  "briefing": "## Situation\nNight, heavy rain, visibility about 5 km. A large, mixed incursion is expected: several swarms, decoys and single drones at once, with birds, civilian drones, our own patrol drones and a friendly helicopter in the same airspace. Rain cuts radar range.\n## Mission\nDefeat the drones that threaten Bridge Post. You have fewer interceptor rounds than hostile drones: prioritise, and use the jammer and spoofer on groups. Do not engage the friendly helicopter or our patrols.\n## ROE\nWEAPONS TIGHT — intercept only tracks you have classified as a threat type and declared HOSTILE. No intercepts inside the marked no-kinetic zones (settlements).\n## Assets\n- Radar, EO/IR camera and RF detector on high ground near the asset\n- RF jammer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 10 s cycle\n- GNSS spoofer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 15 s cycle\n- Interceptor, 1.5 km, 10 rounds, 6 s reload\n## Intel\nAxes are uncertain. The high, RF-loud contacts are likely decoys; the low groups are the attack. A smuggler may try to cross during the confusion.",
